I'd suggest doing that through `config.custom_textobjects` and not via custom mappings. This way it is defined once per texotjbect id, no need for separate 'a'/'i'/'al'/'il'/'an'/'in' mappings. Custom textobjects should follow [specification](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f90b6b820062fc06d6d51ed61a0f9b7f9a13b01b/doc/mini-ai.txt#L256), but looking at [how built-in textobjects are implemented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f90b6b820062fc06d6d51ed61a0f9b7f9a13b01b/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1081-L1124) should get 95% there for this case.

If I correctly understood what you're trying to achieve, the following setup should be all you need:

```lua
require('mini.ai').setup({
  custom_textobjects = {
    ['c'] = { '%b()', '^.().*().$' },
    ['C'] = { '%b()', '^.%s*().-()%s*.$' },
    ['B'] = { { '%b()', '%b[]', '%b{}' }, '^.%s*().-()%s*.$' },
  },
})
```

